2026-09-27T09:27:25.9003386Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9003538Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9003753Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9003952Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004020Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004204Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004298Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004418Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004682Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004838Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9004924Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9005129Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9005258Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9005360Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9005644Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9005901Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9006373Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9006771Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9006857Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9007180Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9007590Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9007809Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9008080Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9008400Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9008470Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9008624Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9008718Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9073800Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9074952Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9075187Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9075593Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9076543Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9077016Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9077429Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9077754Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9078113Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9078202Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9078390Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9078507Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9079820Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9080722Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9081223Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9081898Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:25.9082063Z 
